<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:500px;"><tbody><tr><td><strong>I:</strong></td><td>Their body consists of long, slender thread-like structures called hyphae&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>II:</strong></td><td>The network of hyphae is called mycelium&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>III:</strong></td><td>Hyphae may be continuous tubes filled with multinucleated cytoplasm, these hyphae are coenocytic&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>IV:</strong></td><td>In many cases hyphae have septate or cross walls&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><strong>V:</strong></td><td>The cell wall of fungi are composed by chitin and polysaccharides&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>
